      mp3: 
      ms: 5960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1d05pp5'
    '|b||What survives is a pattern. The state did well where the harm was big and measurable, and it put a price on it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1r6ox8u'
    '|a||And badly where it had to guess what nobody knew, or where a lobby was holding the pen.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1u6njg9'
    '|b||How sure are we? That markets and states both fail, often and expensively: consensus.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:17nb8n9'
    '|a||That pricing a harm beats prescribing the fix: mostly agreed among economists.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1wtrg64'
    '|b||Which failure is worse overall: contested, and maybe the wrong question.':
      mp3: 
